# Keep baseline + reference map; ignore the raw nightly schema snapshots.
schema-2*.json

# drift-2*.md WAS ignored here. It should never have been: 40 drift reports up to
# 6 Aug 2026 are tracked (git ignores the ignore rule once a path is tracked), so
# the rule only ever hid the NEW ones. Every report written from 8 Aug onward sat
# untracked and invisible while the drift routine reported success, and the
# queue-fixer's `git add -A` silently staged nothing. Seven reports were lost to
# this before anyone noticed (finding 20260816-drift-181).
#
# Drift reports compare shipped code against the SOPs. They name files, functions
# and line numbers — no tenant names, no rent figures, no email bodies — so they
# are safe in a public repo, which is why the 40 already there are fine.
#
# If these ever need to stop accumulating, prune old ones deliberately. Do not
# reintroduce an ignore rule: an ignore on a partially-tracked path does not
# reduce noise, it just makes the newest half of the series disappear silently.

# never-commit:begin
#
# Everything between these two markers is a PRIVACY rule, not housekeeping. This
# repo is PUBLIC. .gitignore alone cannot enforce it: once a path is tracked, git
# ignores the ignore rule for ever and prints no warning. That is how
# task-sweep-applied-2026-08-06.json came to sit in a public repo under a comment
# saying NEVER commit these. tests/never-commit-paths.test.js reads the patterns
# between these markers and fails if any of them is tracked.
#
# Add a pattern here only if the file must never be public. Housekeeping ignores
# (things that are merely noisy) belong above the marker.
#
# Task hygiene sweep working files: the work-list carries full inbound email
# bodies, tenant names, rent figures and phone numbers. Only the redacted
# task-sweep-{date}.md report is tracked.
task-sweep-worklist-*.json
task-sweep-decisions-*.json
task-sweep-applied-*.json
task-sweep-pending.json
task-sweep-pending-*.json
# Unredacted companion to the nightly report: names people, suppliers and exact
# sums so Kevin can act. Local only — the tracked .md report stays redacted.
task-sweep-detail-*.md
# never-commit:end
